 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The can top carries the capacitance (100), the voltage (35V) and the series (RVT) in black, with a dark band on the negative side."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "A wound element of anode foil, cathode foil, separator paper and electrolyte sits in an aluminium can sealed by a butyl rubber bung. The can stands on a PPA base plate; the terminals are aluminium with tin-plated copper-clad steel wire."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Hand soldering",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "With a soldering iron, finish each joint at 350 ±5 ℃ within 3 ±1 s unless another specification applies."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Reflow",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Larger cases heat more slowly, the middle of a board runs cooler than its edges, and a large or thick board heats more slowly. The reflow temperature is not set by case size: Φ4 and Φ10 parts can go through the same oven. If a higher temperature than the reflow limits is used, the capacitor temperature and the reflow conditions are measured and reported. Reflow once where possible; where a second pass is needed, both passes' temperatures and the time between them are measured and reported. A third reflow is not allowed."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Cover tape peel",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The cover tape is peeled back at 165° to 180° from the carrier at 300 mm/min; the peel force lies between 0.1 N and 0.7 N."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Tape leader and trailer",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The leader pulled from the reel is 100 to 150 mm long and holds ten or more empty sealed pockets. At the reel core end there is an empty sealed section of at least 60 mm. Along the tape, the trailer is an empty section of 70 mm or more, and the leader is an empty section of 70 mm min within a leader of 150 mm min."
  }
 ],
